{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 35, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a Count of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. Raymond III succeeded his father as Count of Tripoli in 1152. He was still a minor when he ascended to the throne so the regency was held by his mother Hodierna.\n\n*Early Life and Succession*\nRaymond III was born around 1140. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. His father Raymond II was a Count of Tripoli and a member of the House of Toulouse. His mother Hodierna was the daughter of Baldwin II King of Jerusalem and Morphia of Melitene. Raymond III succeeded his father as Count of Tripoli in 1152. He was still a minor when he ascended to the throne so the regency was held by his mother Hodierna.\n\nRaymond III played a significant role in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem. He was a member of the nobility and a cousin of King Baldwin III of Jerusalem. In 1153 he participated in the Siege of Ascalon alongside King Baldwin III. The siege was successful and the city was captured. Raymond III also participated in the Battle of Inab in 1149 alongside King Baldwin III and Prince Raymond of Antioch. The battle was a disaster for the Crusader forces and Prince Raymond of Antioch was killed.\n\n*Marriage and Issue*\nRaymond III married Eschiva of Bures in 1174. Eschiva was the daughter of Walter of Bures and the widow of William of Bures. The marriage was childless. Raymond III died on September 30 1187. He was succeeded by his godson Raymond of Antioch who was the son of Bohemond III Prince of Antioch.\n\n*Legacy*\nRaymond III played a significant role in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem. He was a member of the nobility and a cousin of King Baldwin III of Jerusalem. He participated in several battles and sieges alongside the King of Jerusalem. He also h